 ## Subtopics
 
 ### [MultiFAB Convexification and Parallel Volume Rendering](13298-multifab-convexification-and-parallel-volume-rendering.md)
-A parallel volume rendering strategy for AMR meshes where MultiFABs are processed independently by a GPU renderer and results are combined via MPI reduction.
+A parallel volume rendering strategy for AMR meshes where MultiFABs are processed independently by a GPU renderer and results are combined via MPI reduction. It differs from standard brick renderers by explicitly handling the topological dependencies and non-convexities inherent in AMR grids through a "convexification" preprocessing step, ensuring correct alpha blending for color and emissivity cases. Choose this variant when rendering Adaptive Mesh Refinement datasets that require explicit handling of non-convex grid topologies.
 
